{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>A slave of slaves.</b> Its sense: a slave like one of the slaves. If it were 'slave of the slaves,' it would mean a slave to slaves. The proof: קדש קדשים (Leviticus 6:18) versus בקדש הקדשים (Exodus 26:33)." "And the sense of 'to his brothers' is to Cush, Mizraim, and Put, for they are his father's brothers. Others say the Cushites are slaves because Noah cursed Ham — but they have forgotten, for the first king after the Flood was of Cush, as it is written: 'And the beginning of his kingdom was Babel' (Genesis 10:10)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:00.775224580Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}